# ...except the Vulkan loader shipped for macOS (see README); without this
# exemption the *.dylib rule above silently drops it from commits.
#
# The KosmicKrisp driver beside it is deliberately NOT exempted. It is 15 MB and
# is rebuilt on every Mesa bump, and git keeps every version of a tracked file
# for ever, so committing it here would charge every clone -- and every clone of
# a project using this as a submodule -- for drivers nobody will run again. It
# lives on the `driver` orphan branch, amended in place; `build.sh` and the
# release workflow fetch it, and `vendor-kosmickrisp.sh` publishes it.
!macos-aarch64/libvulkan.1.dylib
/vulkan.c3l
